# AGENTS.md

Guidance for agent sessions working in this repository.

## Hard rules

- Do not execute run, serve, migrate, or build commands. The user runs commands.
- Retain the existing versioned layered structure.
- Verify dependency APIs through Context7 before writing dependency-specific code.
- Do not edit generated Swagger files under `local/docs/` or `cloud/docs/`.
- `shared/` never imports `local/` or `cloud/`.

## Scope

A Go workspace of three modules: `shared/` (entities, enums, common helpers, pkg), `local/` (on-site
service, no auth) and `cloud/` (head-office service with JWT auth, users, roles and schema-scoped reads).
Shared infrastructure on both services: PostgreSQL, OpenTelemetry, slog, Swagger, cobra, and uber/dig.
S3, Infisical and NATS are present in the codebase but commented out until needed.

Every table has one authority side (see README, "How data moves between local and cloud"). Write
endpoints exist only on the authority side; the other side is read-only. Decide the authority before
adding a table.

New backend code follows the existing entity, model, repository, service, handler, and route layers.
Entities live in `shared/entities`; the other layers are duplicated per service under
`<local|cloud>/internal/v1`. Register constructable dependencies in `<service>/internal/container/di.go`
and entities in `<service>/internal/configs/postgres.go`. To add a resource, use the
`apta-go-local-cloud` skill (CRUD scaffolding) instead of hand-copying files.

All database access belongs in repositories. Pass `c.Request.Context()` from Gin handlers to methods
accepting `context.Context`; pass `*gin.Context` only where the method explicitly requires it.
